From: Rayhaan1345 <96483570+Rayhaan1345@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add optional Frobenius-norm clipping of fast-weight
 deltas at inference

The paper (Appendix 9.2) rescales any per-chunk delta whose Frobenius norm exceeds a threshold
tau (1e-5 for Qwen3-4B) before applying it; the released inference code has no such clipping.
Setting ttt_clip in the model config enables it; the default keeps the released behaviour.
---
 inference_model/hf_qwen3/modeling_qwen3.py | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/inference_model/hf_qwen3/modeling_qwen3.py b/inference_model/hf_qwen3/modeling_qwen3.py
index 222861d..b903425 100644
--- a/inference_model/hf_qwen3/modeling_qwen3.py
+++ b/inference_model/hf_qwen3/modeling_qwen3.py
@@ -147,6 +147,13 @@ class Qwen3MLP(nn.Module):
                     )
                 else:
                     dw = contract("c h, c d -> d h", current_h, current_t) * self.ttt_lr
+                # Optional inference-time clipping (paper, Appendix 9.2): rescale a delta whose Frobenius
+                # norm exceeds `ttt_clip` to that norm. Off unless the config sets ttt_clip (as released).
+                clip = getattr(self.config, "ttt_clip", None)
+                if clip is not None:
+                    norm = dw.float().norm()
+                    if norm > clip:
+                        dw = dw * (clip / norm).to(dw.dtype)
                 current_w = current_w + dw
         out = rearrange(y, "b t c d -> b (t c) d")[:, :seq_len, :]
         return out, current_w
